# Run the Agora voice agent

This project runs a local Python session service and browser demo. Agora
Conversational AI runs the speech and reasoning pipeline, and Agora RTC carries
the browser audio. Unmute is not needed at runtime.

## Start locally

Use Python 3.12 or newer. Your Agora project needs Conversational AI enabled,
an App ID, an App Certificate, and access to the managed models below.

```sh
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env
# Fill in AGORA_APP_ID and AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE in .env.
set -a
. ./.env
set +a
python server.py
```

Open http://localhost:8080, allow the microphone, and start a conversation.
The browser joins and publishes audio before the service starts the agent, so
the fixed greeting can be heard. Start acceptance is not evidence of audible
speech; the page reports connected after subscribing to agent audio.

`AGORA_AREA` defaults to `us`; `eu` and `ap` are also accepted. It chooses the
Agora API area. It is not a promise that all model inference remains in that
region. This managed-model example does not support the CN area.

## Supported package behavior

- One agent, one browser realtime_audio channel, and a cascade pipeline.
- Deepgram `nova-3` with language `en`, OpenAI `gpt-4o-mini`, and MiniMax
  `speech_2_6_turbo` with an explicit voice. These use Agora-managed credentials;
  no separate vendor API keys are needed. Voice availability is checked by the
  service during a real conversation, not by the offline compiler.
- System instructions, a fixed agent-first greeting, and an explicit interruption
  setting. Enabled interruption uses Agora's start-of-speech policy.
- `conversation.max_duration` accepts whole seconds from 1s to 600s; omission
  uses 600s. The service enforces this deadline independently of the page.
- Tools, MCP, tasks, handoffs, variables, telephony, video, speech-to-speech
  models, custom model parameters, tracing, capacity and deployment settings
  are refused by this initial target. They are adapter limits, not claims
  about what Agora's products support.

## Session lifecycle

The local service permits five active or prepared sessions. An unused prepared
session expires after 60 seconds. Each started session has its own RTC channel,
browser token and unguessable control key. The browser receives no certificate.
Ending the conversation closes the microphone, leaves RTC and requests agent
cleanup. Repeated stop requests are safe, and failed stops are retried by the
service while it is running. The cloud agent has a 30-second departure idle
limit if its subscribed browser leaves.

A failed or interrupted start may have reached the cloud without returning an
agent ID. The browser leaves on failure, so the departure idle limit remains a
fallback. A killed server cannot enforce its local deadline or retry a stop;
this local demo is not a durable production session controller.

The page ends the conversation before its RTC token lifetime is exhausted. It
does not renew tokens or extend a session. Start a new conversation to continue.
The browser SDK is loaded from a pinned jsDelivr URL and needs network access.

## Container

```sh
docker build -t unmute-agora .
docker run --rm --env-file .env -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 unmute-agora
```

Keep the loopback port binding. This sample uses same-origin localhost checks
and session control keys, not application login or a production ingress. Do not
expose it directly on the public internet. Run one process; sessions live in
memory. Stop the container gracefully to request cleanup of active agents.

`unmute dev` and `unmute deploy` do not launch this target. Run this generated
project using the commands above. Recompile the source package to change the
agent; edits to generated files may be overwritten.

## Verify a real conversation

Use headphones. Confirm the fixed greeting is audible, ask a question, interrupt
a response if interruption is enabled, then end the conversation. Confirm the
microphone is released and the session is stopped in Agora. Record the screen
with sound for review without showing credentials. Offline tests and successful
compilation do not verify model access, audio quality or a completed cloud call.

The interactive starter scaffold does not create Agora packages yet. Copy
`examples/agora-voice` and edit its authored files before compiling.
